{"cklb_version":"1.0","title":"SCC Generated CKLB at: 2026-09-05T10:13:32","id":"93F4AF3B-6BF8-1014-A44C-FF498C8C1731","stigs":[{"display_name":"Mozilla Firefox","version":"6","release_info":"Release: 6 Benchmark Date: 02 Apr 2025","reference_identifier":"5446","uuid":"93E2B29A-6BF8-1014-B7B8-F59365D05FB5","size":34,"rules":[{"potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":[],"fix_text":"Upgrade the version of the browser to an approved version by obtaining software from the vendor or other trusted source.","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000456","id":"V-251545"},"rule_id_src":"SV-251545r961683_rule","responsibility":"","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"93E51AB1-6BF8-1014-873A-A0AF5B892857","rule_version":"FFOX-00-000001","comments":null,"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:23\nResult: notcheckedCriteria                : NOT_TESTED (All child tests must be true.)\nTest                    :   NOT_TESTED (CAT I, V-251545, SV-251545r961683, SRG-APP-000456)\n","mitigation_control":"","discussion":"Using versions of an application that are not supported by the vendor is not permitted. Vendors respond to security flaws with updates and patches. These updates are not available for unsupported versions, which can leave the application vulnerable to attack.","ccis":["CCI-002605"],"group_id":"V-251545","false_positives":"","weight":"10.0","ia_controls":"","rule_title":"The installed version of Firefox must be supported.","third_party_tools":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MOZ_Firefox_Windows_V6R7_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV12-ocil.xml","name":"ocil:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:questionnaire:101"},"classification":"Unclassified","group_title":"SRG-APP-000456","check_content":"Run Firefox. Click the ellipsis button &gt;&gt; Help &gt;&gt; About Firefox, and view the version number.\n\nIf the Firefox version is not a supported version, this is a finding.","group_id_src":"V-251545","severity":"high","status":"not_reviewed","stig_uuid":"93E2B29A-6BF8-1014-B7B8-F59365D05FB5","rule_id":"SV-251545r961683","mitigations":"","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5446"},{"status":"not_a_finding","stig_uuid":"93E2B29A-6BF8-1014-B7B8-F59365D05FB5","mitigations":"","rule_id":"SV-251546r961869","reference_identifier":"5446","documentable":"false","weight":"10.0","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-001453"],"group_id":"V-251546","third_party_tools":"","rule_title":"Firefox must be configured to allow only TLS 1.2 or above.","ia_controls":"","check_content":"Type \"about:policies\" in the browser window. \n\nIf \"SSLVersionMin\" is not displayed under Policy Name or the Policy Value is not \"tls1.2\" or \"tls1.3\", this is a finding.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000560","classification":"Unclassified","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MOZ_Firefox_Windows_V6R7_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV12-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:def:101"},"severity":"high","group_id_src":"V-251546","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:23\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Firefox is configured to allow only TLS 1.2 or above)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:tst:10100 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Firefox is configured to allow only TLS 1.2 or above\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:obj:10100 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'SSLVersionMin'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:ste:10100 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_sz'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must match the pattern 'tls1\\.[23]'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox'\n                        : name equals 'SSLVersionMin'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330997290000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_sz'\n                        : value equals 'tls1.3'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","discussion":"Use of versions prior to TLS 1.2 are not permitted. SSL 2.0 and SSL 3.0 contain a number of security flaws. These versions must be disabled in compliance with the Network Infrastructure and Secure Remote Computing STIGs.","mitigation_control":"","legacy_ids":[],"potential_impacts":"","fix_text":"Windows group policy:\n1. Open the group policy editor tool with \"gpedit.msc\".\n2. Navigate to Policy Path: Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\\nPolicy Name: Minimum SSL version enabled\nPolicy State: Enabled\nPolicy Value: TLS 1.2   (or TLS 1.3)\n\nmacOS \"plist\" file:\nAdd the following:\n&lt;key&gt;SSLVersionMin&lt;/key&gt;\n&lt;string&gt;tls1.2&lt;/string&gt;   (or &lt;string&gt;tls1.3&lt;/string&gt;)\n\nLinux \"policies.json\" file:\nAdd the following in the policies section:\n\"SSLVersionMin\": \"tls1.2\"   or (\"SSLVersionMin\": \"tls1.3\")","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000560","id":"V-251546"},"security_override_guidance":"","responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-251546r961869_rule","comments":null,"rule_version":"FFOX-00-000002","uuid":"93E52796-6BF8-1014-9AD0-EB99701064CD"},{"group_id_src":"V-251547","severity":"medium","classification":"Unclassified","group_title":"SRG-APP-000177","check_content":"Type \"about:policies\" in the browser address bar. \n\nIf \"Preferences\" is not displayed under Policy Name and the Policy Value does not include \"security.default_personal_cert\" with a value of \"Ask Every Time\" and status of \"locked\", this is a finding.","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:def:251547","href":"U_MOZ_Firefox_Windows_V6R7_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV12-oval2.xml"},"ia_controls":"","third_party_tools":"","rule_title":"Firefox must be configured to ask which certificate to present to a website when a certificate is required.","weight":"10.0","false_positives":"","group_id":"V-251547","ccis":["CCI-000187"],"documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5446","rule_id":"SV-251547r1067550","mitigations":"","stig_uuid":"93E2B29A-6BF8-1014-B7B8-F59365D05FB5","status":"open","rule_version":"FFOX-00-000003","comments":null,"uuid":"93E53119-6BF8-1014-9170-EFC6FCD774EA","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id_src":"SV-251547r1067550_rule","responsibility":"","fix_text":"Windows group policy:\n1. Open the group policy editor tool with \"gpedit.msc\".\n2. Navigate to Policy Path: Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\\nPolicy Name: Preferences\nPolicy State: Enabled\nPolicy Value:\n{\n  \"security.default_personal_cert\": {\n    \"Value\": \"Ask Every Time\",\n    \"Status\": \"locked\"\n  }\n}\n\nmacOS \"plist\" file:\nAdd the following:\n&lt;key&gt;Preferences&lt;/key&gt;\n&lt;dict&gt;\n  &lt;key&gt;security.default_personal_cert&lt;/key&gt;\n  &lt;dict&gt;\n    &lt;key&gt;Value&lt;/key&gt;\n    &lt;string&gt;Ask Every Time&lt;/string&gt;\n    &lt;key&gt;Status&lt;/key&gt;\n    &lt;string&gt;locked&lt;/string&gt;\n  &lt;/dict&gt;\n&lt;/dict&gt;\n\nLinux \"policies.json\" file:\nAdd the following in the policies section:\n\"Preferences\": {\n  \"security.default_personal_cert\": {\n    \"Value\": \"Ask Every Time\",\n    \"Status\": \"locked\"\n  }\n}","group_tree":{"id":"V-251547","title":"SRG-APP-000177"},"legacy_ids":[],"potential_impacts":"","discussion":"When a website asks for a certificate for user authentication, Firefox must be configured to have the user choose which certificate to present. Websites within DOD require user authentication for access, which increases security for DOD information. Access will be denied to the user if certificate management is not configured.","mitigation_control":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:23\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Firefox must be configured to ask which certificate to present to a website when a certificate is required.)\nResult Analysis         :        '' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to '\"security.default_personal_cert\": \\{    \"Value\": \"Ask Every Time\",    \"Status\": \"locked\"  }' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:tst:25154701 (variable_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Firefox must be configured to ask which certificate to present to a website when a certificate is required.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:obj:25154701 (variable_object)\nObject Comment          : Merged format of Firefox SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\Preferences Multi-String registry key\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'var_ref' must be equal to 'oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:var:25154701'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:ste:25154701 (variable_state)\nState Comment           : Check that the security.default_personal_cert is ask every time, and locked\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must match the pattern '\"security.default_personal_cert\": \\{    \"Value\": \"Ask Every Time\",    \"Status\": \"locked\"  }'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : var_ref equals 'oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:var:25154701'\n                        : value equals ''\n\nResult Analysis         : '' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to '\"security.default_personal_cert\": \\{    \"Value\": \"Ask Every Time\",    \"Status\": \"locked\"  }' \n"},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:23\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Firefox must be configured to not automatically check for updated versions of installed search plugins.)\nResult Analysis         :        '' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to '\"browser.search.update\": \\{    \"Value\": false,    \"Status\": \"locked\"  }' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:tst:25154801 (variable_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Firefox must be configured to not automatically check for updated versions of installed search plugins.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:obj:25154801 (variable_object)\nObject Comment          : Merged format of Firefox SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\Preferences Multi-String registry key\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'var_ref' must be equal to 'oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:var:25154801'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:ste:25154801 (variable_state)\nState Comment           : Verify that browser.search.update is set to false and locked\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must match the pattern '\"browser.search.update\": \\{    \"Value\": false,    \"Status\": \"locked\"  }'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : var_ref equals 'oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:var:25154801'\n                        : value equals ''\n\nResult Analysis         : '' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to '\"browser.search.update\": \\{    \"Value\": false,    \"Status\": \"locked\"  }' \n","discussion":"Updates must be controlled and installed from authorized and trusted servers. This setting overrides a number of other settings that may direct the application to access external URLs.","mitigation_control":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-251548"},"fix_text":"Windows group policy:\n1. Open the group policy editor tool with \"gpedit.msc\".\n2. Navigate to Policy Path: Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\\nPolicy Name: Preferences\nPolicy State: Enabled\nPolicy Value:\n{\n  \"browser.search.update\": {\n    \"Value\": false,\n    \"Status\": \"locked\"\n  }\n}\n\nmacOS \"plist\" file:\nAdd the following:\n&lt;key&gt;Preferences&lt;/key&gt;\n&lt;dict&gt;\n  &lt;key&gt;browser.search.update&lt;/key&gt;\n  &lt;dict&gt;\n    &lt;key&gt;Value&lt;/key&gt;\n    &lt;false/&gt;\n    &lt;key&gt;Status&lt;/key&gt;\n    &lt;string&gt;locked&lt;/string&gt;\n  &lt;/dict&gt;\n&lt;/dict&gt;\n\nLinux \"policies.json\" file:\nAdd the following in the policies section:\n\"Preferences\": {\n  \"browser.search.update\": {\n    \"Value\": false,\n    \"Status\": \"locked\"\n  }\n}","legacy_ids":[],"potential_impacts":"","comments":null,"rule_version":"FFOX-00-000004","uuid":"93E56BD2-6BF8-1014-B25A-FF84447F28E4","security_override_guidance":"","responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-251548r1067552_rule","stig_uuid":"93E2B29A-6BF8-1014-B7B8-F59365D05FB5","status":"open","reference_identifier":"5446","documentable":"false","mitigations":"","rule_id":"SV-251548r1067552","rule_title":"Firefox must be configured to not automatically check for updated versions of installed search plugins.","third_party_tools":"","ia_controls":"","false_positives":"","weight":"10.0","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"group_id":"V-251548","severity":"medium","group_id_src":"V-251548","check_content":"Type \"about:policies\" in the browser address bar. \n\nIf \"Preferences\" is not displayed under Policy Name or the Policy Value does not include \"browser.search.update\" with a value of  \"false\" and status of \"locked\", this is a finding.","classification":"Unclassified","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MOZ_Firefox_Windows_V6R7_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV12-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:def:251548"}},{"discussion":"Set this to false to disable checking for updated versions of the Extensions/Themes. Automatic updates from untrusted sites puts the enclave at risk of attack and may override security settings.","mitigation_control":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:23\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Firefox is configured to not automatically update installed add-ons and plugins)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:tst:10400 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Firefox is configured to not automatically update installed add-ons and plugins\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:obj:10400 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'ExtensionUpdate'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:ste:2 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox'\n                        : name equals 'ExtensionUpdate'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330997290000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","security_override_guidance":"","responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-251549r960963_rule","rule_version":"FFOX-00-000005","comments":null,"uuid":"93E58030-6BF8-1014-B66B-882A52116FD8","legacy_ids":[],"potential_impacts":"","fix_text":"Windows group policy:\n1. Open the group policy editor tool with \"gpedit.msc\".\n2. Navigate to Policy Path: Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\Extensions\nPolicy Name: Extension Update\nPolicy State: Disabled\n\nmacOS \"plist\" file:\nAdd the following:\n&lt;key&gt;ExtensionUpdate&lt;/key&gt;\n&lt;false/&gt;\n\nLinux \"policies.json\" file:\nAdd the following in the policies section:\n\"ExtensionUpdate\": false","group_tree":{"id":"V-251549","title":"SRG-APP-000141"},"rule_id":"SV-251549r960963","mitigations":"","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5446","status":"not_a_finding","stig_uuid":"93E2B29A-6BF8-1014-B7B8-F59365D05FB5","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","classification":"Unclassified","check_content":"Type \"about:policies\" in the browser window.\n\nIf \"ExtensionUpdate\" is not displayed under Policy Name or the Policy Value is not \"false\", this is a finding.","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:def:104","href":"U_MOZ_Firefox_Windows_V6R7_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV12-oval.xml"},"group_id_src":"V-251549","severity":"medium","false_positives":"","weight":"10.0","group_id":"V-251549","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"ia_controls":"","rule_title":"Firefox must be configured to not automatically update installed add-ons and plugins.","third_party_tools":""},{"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000278","id":"V-251550"},"fix_text":"Remove any unauthorized extensions from the auto-download list.","potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":[],"uuid":"93E5C825-6BF8-1014-963E-80F081EC5C8A","rule_version":"FFOX-00-000006","comments":null,"responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-251550r961194_rule","security_override_guidance":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:23\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Check all Firefox Profiles for MIME types)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:tst:25155001 (textfilecontent54_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Check all Firefox Profiles for MIME types\nCheck Existence         : Zero or more collected items may exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:obj:25155001 (textfilecontent54_object)\nObject Comment          : Gather MIME Types and Actions\nObject Requirement      : for filepath, all of the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     filepath must be equal to 'C:\\Users\\Degthat\\AppData\\Roaming\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\Profiles\\iri0mens.default-release\\handlers.json'\nObject Requirement      : for pattern, all of the following must be true:\nObject Requirement      :     pattern must be equal to '(?i)\":\\{\"action\":(\\d),\"extensions\":\\[\"HTA\"\\]'\nObject Requirement      :     pattern must be equal to '(?i)\":\\{\"action\":(\\d),\"extensions\":\\[\"JSE\"\\]'\nObject Requirement      :     pattern must be equal to '(?i)\":\\{\"action\":(\\d),\"extensions\":\\[\"JS\"\\]'\nObject Requirement      :     pattern must be equal to '(?i)\":\\{\"action\":(\\d),\"extensions\":\\[\"MOCHA\"\\]'\nObject Requirement      :     pattern must be equal to '(?i)\":\\{\"action\":(\\d),\"extensions\":\\[\"SHS\"\\]'\nObject Requirement      :     pattern must be equal to '(?i)\":\\{\"action\":(\\d),\"extensions\":\\[\"VBE\"\\]'\nObject Requirement      :     pattern must be equal to '(?i)\":\\{\"action\":(\\d),\"extensions\":\\[\"VBS\"\\]'\nObject Requirement      :     pattern must be equal to '(?i)\":\\{\"action\":(\\d),\"extensions\":\\[\"SCT\"\\]'\nObject Requirement      :     pattern must be equal to '(?i)\":\\{\"action\":(\\d),\"extensions\":\\[\"WSC\"\\]'\nObject Requirement      :     pattern must be equal to '(?i)\":\\{\"action\":(\\d),\"extensions\":\\[\"FDF\"\\]'\nObject Requirement      :     pattern must be equal to '(?i)\":\\{\"action\":(\\d),\"extensions\":\\[\"XFDF\"\\]'\nObject Requirement      :     pattern must be equal to '(?i)\":\\{\"action\":(\\d),\"extensions\":\\[\"LSL\"\\]'\nObject Requirement      :     pattern must be equal to '(?i)\":\\{\"action\":(\\d),\"extensions\":\\[\"LSO\"\\]'\nObject Requirement      :     pattern must be equal to '(?i)\":\\{\"action\":(\\d),\"extensions\":\\[\"LSS\"\\]'\nObject Requirement      :     pattern must be equal to '(?i)\":\\{\"action\":(\\d),\"extensions\":\\[\"IQY\"\\]'\nObject Requirement      :     pattern must be equal to '(?i)\":\\{\"action\":(\\d),\"extensions\":\\[\"RQY\"\\]'\nObject Requirement      :     pattern must be equal to '(?i)\":\\{\"action\":(\\d),\"extensions\":\\[\"DOS\"\\]'\nObject Requirement      :     pattern must be equal to '(?i)\":\\{\"action\":(\\d),\"extensions\":\\[\"BAT\"\\]'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'instance' must be greater than or equal to '1'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:ste:25155001 (textfilecontent54_state)\nState Comment           : Check firefox mime type actions\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'subexpression' must match the pattern '0|1'\n","mitigation_control":"","discussion":"Some files can be downloaded or execute without user interaction. This setting ensures these files are not downloaded and executed.","ia_controls":"","third_party_tools":"","rule_title":"Firefox must be configured to not automatically execute or download MIME types that are not authorized for auto-download.","ccis":["CCI-001242"],"group_id":"V-251550","weight":"10.0","false_positives":"","group_id_src":"V-251550","severity":"medium","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MOZ_Firefox_Windows_V6R7_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV12-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:def:251550"},"classification":"Unclassified","group_title":"SRG-APP-000278","check_content":"Type \"about:preferences\" in the browser address bar. \n\nType \"Applications\" in the Find bar in the upper-right corner. \n\nDetermine if any of the following file extensions are listed: HTA, JSE, JS, MOCHA, SHS, VBE, VBS, SCT, WSC, FDF, XFDF, LSL, LSO, LSS, IQY, RQY, DOS, BAT, PS, EPS, WCH, WCM, WB1, WB3, WCH, WCM, AD.\n\nIf the entry exists and the \"Action\" is \"Save File\" or \"Always Ask\", this is not a finding.\n \nIf an extension exists and the entry in the Action column is associated with an application that does/can execute the code, this is a finding.","stig_uuid":"93E2B29A-6BF8-1014-B7B8-F59365D05FB5","status":"not_a_finding","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5446","rule_id":"SV-251550r961194","mitigations":""},{"weight":"10.0","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"group_id":"V-251551","third_party_tools":"","rule_title":"Firefox must be configured to disable form fill assistance.","ia_controls":"","check_content":"Type \"about:policies\" in the browser window. \n\nIf \"DisableFormHistory\" is not displayed under Policy Name or the Policy Value is not \"true\", this is a finding.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","classification":"Unclassified","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MOZ_Firefox_Windows_V6R7_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV12-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:def:106"},"severity":"medium","group_id_src":"V-251551","status":"not_a_finding","stig_uuid":"93E2B29A-6BF8-1014-B7B8-F59365D05FB5","mitigations":"","rule_id":"SV-251551r960963","reference_identifier":"5446","documentable":"false","legacy_ids":[],"potential_impacts":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-251551"},"fix_text":"Windows group policy:\n1. Open the group policy editor tool with \"gpedit.msc\".\n2. Navigate to Policy Path: Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Mozilla\\Firefox\nPolicy Name: Disable Form History\nPolicy State: Enabled\n\nmacOS \"plist\" file:\nAdd the following:\n&lt;key&gt;DisableFormHistory&lt;/key&gt;\n&lt;true/&gt;\n\nLinux \"policies.json\" file:\nAdd the following in the policies section:\n\"DisableFormHistory\": true","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id_src":"SV-251551r960963_rule","responsibility":"","comments":null,"rule_version":"FFOX-00-000007","uuid":"93E5D6B1-6BF8-1014-915E-DE612173BD6A","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:23\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Firefox is configured to disable form fill assistance)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:tst:10600 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Firefox is configured to disable form fill assistance\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:obj:10600 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisableFormHistory'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:ste:1 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox'\n                        : name equals 'DisableFormHistory'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330997290000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","discussion":"To protect privacy and sensitive data, Firefox provides the ability to configure the program so that data entered into forms is not saved. This mitigates the risk of a website gleaning private information from prefilled information.","mitigation_control":""},{"rule_id_src":"SV-251552r960963_rule","responsibility":"","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"93E5DD45-6BF8-1014-B427-82A001C6F72F","comments":null,"rule_version":"FFOX-00-000008","potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":[],"fix_text":"Windows group policy:\n1. Open the group policy editor tool with \"gpedit.msc\".\n2. Navigate to Policy Path: Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Mozilla\\Firefox\nPolicy Name: PasswordManager\nPolicy State: Disabled\n\nmacOS \"plist\" file:\nAdd the following:\n&lt;key&gt;PasswordManagerEnabled&lt;/key&gt;\n&lt;false/&gt;\n\nLinux \"policies.json\" file:\nAdd the following in the policies section:\n\"PasswordManagerEnabled\": false","group_tree":{"id":"V-251552","title":"SRG-APP-000141"},"mitigation_control":"","discussion":"Firefox can be set to store passwords for sites visited by the user. These individual passwords are stored in a file and can be protected by a master password. Autofill of the password can then be enabled when the site is visited. This feature could also be used to autofill the certificate PIN, which could lead to compromise of DoD information.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:23\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Firefox is configured to not use a password store with or without a master password)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\PasswordManagerEnabled'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:tst:10700 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Firefox is configured to not use a password store with or without a master password\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:obj:10700 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'PasswordManagerEnabled'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:ste:2 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\PasswordManagerEnabled'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:def:107","href":"U_MOZ_Firefox_Windows_V6R7_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV12-oval.xml"},"check_content":"Type \"about:policies\" in the browser window. \n\nIf \"PasswordManagerEnabled\" is not displayed under Policy Name or the Policy Value is not \"false\", this is a finding.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","classification":"Unclassified","severity":"medium","group_id_src":"V-251552","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"group_id":"V-251552","weight":"10.0","false_positives":"","third_party_tools":"","rule_title":"Firefox must be configured to not use a password store with or without a master password.","ia_controls":"","mitigations":"","rule_id":"SV-251552r960963","reference_identifier":"5446","documentable":"false","status":"open","stig_uuid":"93E2B29A-6BF8-1014-B7B8-F59365D05FB5"},{"discussion":"Pop-up windows may be used to launch an attack within a new browser window with altered settings. This setting blocks pop-up windows created while the page is loading.","mitigation_control":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:23\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Firefox is configured to block pop-up windows)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\PopupBlocking\\Default'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :   false (Firefox pop-up preferences are locked)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\PopupBlocking\\Locked'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:tst:10800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Firefox is configured to block pop-up windows\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:obj:10800 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\PopupBlocking'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'Default'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:ste:1 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\PopupBlocking\\Default'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:tst:10801 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Firefox pop-up preferences are locked\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:obj:10801 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\PopupBlocking'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'Locked'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:ste:1 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\PopupBlocking\\Locked'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id_src":"SV-251553r960963_rule","responsibility":"","comments":null,"rule_version":"FFOX-00-000009","uuid":"93E5E27C-6BF8-1014-A386-FC04EB2154CE","legacy_ids":[],"potential_impacts":"","fix_text":"Windows group policy:\n1. Open the group policy editor tool with \"gpedit.msc\".\n2. Navigate to Policy Path: Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\Popups\nPolicy Name: Block pop-ups from websites\nPolicy State: Enabled\n\nPolicy Name: Do not allow preferences to be changed\nPolicy State: Enabled\n\nOptional:\nPolicy Name: Allowed Sites\nPolicy State: Enabled\nClick \"Show...\" and enter a list of websites to be allowlisted.\n\nmacOS \"plist\" file:\nAdd the following:\n&lt;key&gt;PopupBlocking&lt;/key&gt;\n  &lt;dict&gt;\n    &lt;key&gt;Allow&lt;/key&gt;\n    &lt;array&gt;\n      &lt;string&gt;http://example.mil&lt;/string&gt;\n      &lt;string&gt;http://example.gov&lt;/string&gt;\n    &lt;/array&gt;\n    &lt;key&gt;Default&lt;/key&gt;\n    &lt;true/&gt;\n    &lt;key&gt;Locked&lt;/key&gt;\n    &lt;true/&gt;\n  &lt;/dict&gt;\n\nLinux \"policies.json\" file:\nAdd the following in the policies section:\n\"PopupBlocking\": {\n      \"Allow\": [\"http://example.mil/\",\n                \"http://example.gov/\"],\n      \"Default\": true,\n      \"Locked\": true}","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-251553"},"mitigations":"","rule_id":"SV-251553r960963","reference_identifier":"5446","documentable":"false","status":"open","stig_uuid":"93E2B29A-6BF8-1014-B7B8-F59365D05FB5","check_content":"Type \"about:policies\" in the browser address bar.\n\nIf \"PopupBlocking\" is not displayed under Policy Name or the Policy Value is not \"Default\" \"true\", this is a finding.\nIf \"PopupBlocking\" is not displayed under Policy Name or the Policy Value is not \"Locked\" \"true\", this is a finding.\n\n\"PopupBlocking\" \"Enabled\" may be used to specify an allowlist of sites where pop-ups are desired, this is optional.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","classification":"Unclassified","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:def:108","href":"U_MOZ_Firefox_Windows_V6R7_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV12-oval.xml"},"severity":"medium","group_id_src":"V-251553","weight":"10.0","false_positives":"","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"group_id":"V-251553","third_party_tools":"","rule_title":"Firefox must be configured to block pop-up windows.","ia_controls":""},{"responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-251554r1067554_rule","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"93E5E79C-6BF8-1014-91AA-AD593E64F2A6","comments":null,"rule_version":"FFOX-00-000010","potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-251554"},"fix_text":"Windows group policy:\n1. Open the group policy editor tool with \"gpedit.msc\".\n2. Navigate to Policy Path: Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\\nPolicy Name: Preferences\nPolicy State: Enabled\nPolicy Value:\n{\n  \"dom.disable_window_move_resize\": {\n    \"Value\": true,\n    \"Status\": \"locked\"\n  }\n}\n\nmacOS \"plist\" file:\nAdd the following:\n&lt;key&gt;Preferences&lt;/key&gt;\n&lt;dict&gt;\n  &lt;key&gt;dom.disable_window_move_resize&lt;/key&gt;\n  &lt;dict&gt;\n    &lt;key&gt;Value&lt;/key&gt;\n    &lt;true/&gt;\n    &lt;key&gt;Status&lt;/key&gt;\n    &lt;string&gt;locked&lt;/string&gt;\n  &lt;/dict&gt;\n&lt;/dict&gt;\n\nLinux \"policies.json\" file:\nAdd the following in the policies section:\n\"Preferences\": {\n  \"dom.disable_window_move_resize\": {\n    \"Value\": true,\n    \"Status\": \"locked\"\n  }\n}","mitigation_control":"","discussion":"JavaScript can make changes to the browser's appearance. This activity can help disguise an attack taking place in a minimized background window. Configure the browser setting to prevent scripts on visited websites from moving and resizing browser windows.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:23\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Firefox must be configured to prevent JavaScript from moving or resizing windows.)\nResult Analysis         :        '' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to '\"dom.disable_window_move_resize\": \\{    \"Value\": true,    \"Status\": \"locked\"  }' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:tst:25155401 (variable_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Firefox must be configured to prevent JavaScript from moving or resizing windows.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:obj:25155401 (variable_object)\nObject Comment          : Merged format of Firefox SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\Preferences Multi-String registry key\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'var_ref' must be equal to 'oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:var:25155401'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:ste:25155401 (variable_state)\nState Comment           : Verify dom.disable_window_move_resize is set to true and locked\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must match the pattern '\"dom.disable_window_move_resize\": \\{    \"Value\": true,    \"Status\": \"locked\"  }'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : var_ref equals 'oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:var:25155401'\n                        : value equals ''\n\nResult Analysis         : '' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to '\"dom.disable_window_move_resize\": \\{    \"Value\": true,    \"Status\": \"locked\"  }' \n","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MOZ_Firefox_Windows_V6R7_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV12-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:def:251554"},"check_content":"Type \"about:policies\" in the browser address bar. \n\nIf \"Preferences\" is not displayed under Policy Name or the Policy Value does not include \"dom.disable_window_move_resize\" with a value of  \"true\" and status of \"locked\", this is a finding.","classification":"Unclassified","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","severity":"medium","group_id_src":"V-251554","group_id":"V-251554","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"weight":"10.0","false_positives":"","rule_title":"Firefox must be configured to prevent JavaScript from moving or resizing windows.","third_party_tools":"","ia_controls":"","mitigations":"","rule_id":"SV-251554r1067554","reference_identifier":"5446","documentable":"false","status":"open","stig_uuid":"93E2B29A-6BF8-1014-B7B8-F59365D05FB5"},{"false_positives":"","weight":"10.0","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"group_id":"V-251555","ia_controls":"","rule_title":"Firefox must be configured to prevent JavaScript from raising or lowering windows.","third_party_tools":"","classification":"Unclassified","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","check_content":"Type \"about:policies\" in the browser address bar. \n\nIf \"Preferences\" is not displayed under Policy Name or the Policy Value does not include \"dom.disable_window_flip\" with a value of \"true\" and status of \"locked\", this is a finding.","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MOZ_Firefox_Windows_V6R7_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV12-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:def:251555"},"group_id_src":"V-251555","severity":"medium","status":"open","stig_uuid":"93E2B29A-6BF8-1014-B7B8-F59365D05FB5","rule_id":"SV-251555r1067556","mitigations":"","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5446","legacy_ids":[],"potential_impacts":"","fix_text":"Windows group policy:\n1. Open the group policy editor tool with \"gpedit.msc\".\n2. Navigate to Policy Path: Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\\nPolicy Name: Preferences\nPolicy State: Enabled\nPolicy Value:\n{\n  \"dom.disable_window_flip\": {\n    \"Value\": true,\n    \"Status\": \"locked\"\n  }\n}\n\nmacOS \"plist\" file:\nAdd the following:\n&lt;key&gt;Preferences&lt;/key&gt;\n&lt;dict&gt;\n  &lt;key&gt;dom.disable_window_flip&lt;/key&gt;\n  &lt;dict&gt;\n    &lt;key&gt;Value&lt;/key&gt;\n    &lt;true/&gt;\n    &lt;key&gt;Status&lt;/key&gt;\n    &lt;string&gt;locked&lt;/string&gt;\n  &lt;/dict&gt;\n&lt;/dict&gt;\n\nLinux \"policies.json\" file:\nAdd the following in the policies section:\n\"Preferences\": {\n  \"dom.disable_window_flip\": {\n    \"Value\": true,\n    \"Status\": \"locked\"\n  }\n}","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-251555"},"security_override_guidance":"","rule_id_src":"SV-251555r1067556_rule","responsibility":"","rule_version":"FFOX-00-000011","comments":null,"uuid":"93E5EC7D-6BF8-1014-8827-83E0C27EDE4A","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:23\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Firefox must be configured to prevent JavaScript from raising or lowering windows)\nResult Analysis         :        '' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to '\"dom.disable_window_flip\": \\{    \"Value\": true,    \"Status\": \"locked\"  }' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:tst:25155501 (variable_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Firefox must be configured to prevent JavaScript from raising or lowering windows\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:obj:25155501 (variable_object)\nObject Comment          : Merged format of Firefox SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\Preferences Multi-String registry key\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'var_ref' must be equal to 'oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:var:25155501'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:ste:25155501 (variable_state)\nState Comment           : Verify dom.disable_window_flip is set to true and locked\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must match the pattern '\"dom.disable_window_flip\": \\{    \"Value\": true,    \"Status\": \"locked\"  }'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : var_ref equals 'oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:var:25155501'\n                        : value equals ''\n\nResult Analysis         : '' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to '\"dom.disable_window_flip\": \\{    \"Value\": true,    \"Status\": \"locked\"  }' \n","discussion":"JavaScript can raise and lower browser windows to cause improper input. Configure the browser setting to prevent scripts on visited websites from raising and lowering browser windows.","mitigation_control":""},{"mitigations":"","rule_id":"SV-251557r960963","reference_identifier":"5446","documentable":"false","status":"open","stig_uuid":"93E2B29A-6BF8-1014-B7B8-F59365D05FB5","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MOZ_Firefox_Windows_V6R7_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV12-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:def:112"},"check_content":"Type \"about:policies\" in the browser address bar. \n\nIf \"InstallAddonsPermission\" is not displayed under Policy Name or the Policy Value is not \"Default\" \"false\", this is a finding.","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","classification":"Unclassified","severity":"medium","group_id_src":"V-251557","group_id":"V-251557","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"false_positives":"","weight":"10.0","third_party_tools":"","rule_title":"Firefox must be configured to disable the installation of extensions.","ia_controls":"","mitigation_control":"","discussion":"A browser extension is a program that has been installed into the browser to add functionality. Where a plug-in interacts only with a web page and usually a third-party external application (e.g., Flash, Adobe Reader), an extension interacts with the browser program itself. Extensions are not embedded in web pages and must be downloaded and installed in order to work. Extensions allow browsers to avoid restrictions that apply to web pages. \n\nFor example, an extension can be written to combine data from multiple domains and present it when a certain page is accessed, which can be considered cross-site scripting. If a browser is configured to allow unrestricted use of extensions, plug-ins can be loaded and installed from malicious sources and used on the browser.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:23\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Firefox is configured to disable the installation of extensions)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\InstallAddonsPermission\\Default'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:tst:11200 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Firefox is configured to disable the installation of extensions\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:obj:11200 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\InstallAddonsPermission'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'Default'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:ste:2 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\InstallAddonsPermission\\Default'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n","responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-251557r960963_rule","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"93E5F160-6BF8-1014-80E1-FB88A216E175","comments":null,"rule_version":"FFOX-00-000013","potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":[],"fix_text":"Windows group policy:\n1. Open the group policy editor tool with \"gpedit.msc\".\n2. Navigate to Policy Path: Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\Addons\nPolicy Name: Allow add-on installs from websites\nPolicy State: Disabled\n\nmacOS \"plist\" file:\nAdd the following:\n&lt;key&gt;InstallAddonsPermission&lt;/key&gt;\n&lt;false/&gt;\n\nLinux \"policies.json\" file:\nAdd the following in the policies section:\n\"InstallAddonsPermission\": {\n      \"Default\": false\n}","group_tree":{"id":"V-251557","title":"SRG-APP-000141"}},{"group_id_src":"V-251558","severity":"medium","classification":"Unclassified","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","check_content":"Type \"about:policies\" in the browser window. \n\nIf \"DisableTelemetry\" is not displayed under Policy Name or the Policy Value is not \"true\", this is a finding.","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MOZ_Firefox_Windows_V6R7_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV12-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:def:113"},"ia_controls":"","third_party_tools":"","rule_title":"Background submission of information to Mozilla must be disabled.","false_positives":"","weight":"10.0","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"group_id":"V-251558","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5446","rule_id":"SV-251558r960963","mitigations":"","stig_uuid":"93E2B29A-6BF8-1014-B7B8-F59365D05FB5","status":"not_a_finding","rule_version":"FFOX-00-000014","comments":null,"uuid":"93E5F643-6BF8-1014-A555-EC283833B316","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id_src":"SV-251558r960963_rule","responsibility":"","fix_text":"Windows group policy:\n1. Open the group policy editor tool with \"gpedit.msc\".\n2. Navigate to Policy Path: Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Mozilla\\Firefox\nPolicy Name: Disable Telemetry\nPolicy State: Enabled\n\nmacOS \"plist\" file:\nAdd the following:\n&lt;key&gt;DisableTelemetry&lt;/key&gt;\n&lt;true/&gt;\n\nLinux \"policies.json\" file:\nAdd the following in the policies section:\n\"DisableTelemetry\": true","group_tree":{"id":"V-251558","title":"SRG-APP-000141"},"legacy_ids":[],"potential_impacts":"","discussion":"Firefox by default sends information about Firefox to Mozilla servers. There should be no background submission of technical and other information from DoD computers to Mozilla with portions posted publicly.","mitigation_control":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:23\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Background submission of information to Mozilla is disabled)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:tst:11300 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Background submission of information to Mozilla is disabled\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:obj:11300 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisableTelemetry'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:ste:1 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox'\n                        : name equals 'DisableTelemetry'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330997290000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n"},{"discussion":"Information needed by an attacker to begin looking for possible vulnerabilities in a web browser includes any information about the web browser and plug-ins or modules being used. When debugging or trace information is enabled in a production web browser, information about the web browser, such as web browser type, version, patches installed, plug-ins and modules installed, type of code being used by the hosted application, and any back ends being used for data storage may be displayed. Because this information may be placed in logs and general messages during normal operation of the web browser, an attacker does not have to cause an error condition to gain this information.","mitigation_control":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:23\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Firefox development tools are disabled)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:tst:11400 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Firefox development tools are disabled\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:obj:11400 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisableDeveloperTools'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:ste:1 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox'\n                        : name equals 'DisableDeveloperTools'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330997290000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","comments":null,"rule_version":"FFOX-00-000015","uuid":"93E5FB53-6BF8-1014-A280-CC4C345B58CD","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id_src":"SV-251559r961167_rule","responsibility":"","fix_text":"Windows group policy:\n1. Open the group policy editor tool with \"gpedit.msc\".\n2. Navigate to Policy Path: Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Mozilla\\Firefox\nPolicy Name: Disable Developer Tools\nPolicy State: Enabled\n\nmacOS \"plist\" file:\nAdd the following:\n&lt;key&gt;DisableDeveloperTools&lt;/key&gt;\n&lt;true/&gt;\n\nLinux \"policies.json\" file:\nAdd the following in the policies section:\n\"DisableDeveloperTools\": true","group_tree":{"id":"V-251559","title":"SRG-APP-000266"},"legacy_ids":[],"potential_impacts":"","reference_identifier":"5446","documentable":"false","mitigations":"","rule_id":"SV-251559r961167","stig_uuid":"93E2B29A-6BF8-1014-B7B8-F59365D05FB5","status":"not_a_finding","severity":"low","group_id_src":"V-251559","check_content":"Type \"about:policies\" in the browser window. \n\nIf \"DisableDeveloperTools\" is not displayed under Policy Name or the Policy Value is not \"true\", this is a finding.","classification":"Unclassified","group_title":"SRG-APP-000266","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MOZ_Firefox_Windows_V6R7_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV12-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:def:114"},"third_party_tools":"","rule_title":"Firefox development tools must be disabled.","ia_controls":"","weight":"10.0","false_positives":"","group_id":"V-251559","ccis":["CCI-001312"]},{"group_title":"SRG-APP-000175","classification":"Unclassified","check_content":"Type \"about:preferences#privacy\" in the browser window. \n\nScroll down to the bottom and select \"View Certificates...\".\n\nIn the Certificate Manager window, select the \"Authorities\" tab.\n\nScroll through the Certificate Name list to the U.S. Government heading. Look for the entries for DOD Root CA 3, DOD Root CA 4, and DOD Root CA 5.\n\nIf there are entries for DOD Root CA 3, DOD Root CA 4, and DOD Root CA 5, select them individually.\n\nClick \"View\".\n\nVerify the issuer name is \"US Government\".\n\nIf there are no entries for the appropriate DOD root certificates, this is a finding. If other AO-approved certificates are used, this is not a finding. If SIPRNet-specific certificates are used, this is not a finding.\n\nNote: In a Windows environment, use of policy setting \"security.enterprise_roots.enabled=true\" will point Firefox to the Windows Trusted Root Certification Authority Store. This is not a finding. It can also be set via the policy Certificates &gt;&gt; ImportEnterpriseRoots, which can be verified via \"about:policies\".","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MOZ_Firefox_Windows_V6R7_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV12-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:def:251560"},"group_id_src":"V-251560","severity":"medium","false_positives":"","weight":"10.0","ccis":["CCI-000185"],"group_id":"V-251560","ia_controls":"","third_party_tools":"","rule_title":"Firefox must have the DOD root certificates installed.","rule_id":"SV-251560r1067559","mitigations":"","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5446","status":"open","stig_uuid":"93E2B29A-6BF8-1014-B7B8-F59365D05FB5","security_override_guidance":"","responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-251560r1067559_rule","rule_version":"FFOX-00-000016","comments":null,"uuid":"93E60026-6BF8-1014-A81A-A66868849088","legacy_ids":[],"potential_impacts":"","fix_text":"Install the DOD root certificates. Other AO-approved certificates may also be used. Certificates designed for SIPRNet may be used as appropriate.\n\nOn Windows, import certificates from the operating system by using Certificates &gt;&gt; Import Enterprise Roots (Certificates) via policy or Group Policy Object (GPO).","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000175","id":"V-251560"},"discussion":"The DOD root certificates will ensure that the trust chain is established for server certificates issued from the DOD Certificate Authority (CA).","mitigation_control":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:23\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Firefox must have the DOD root certificates installed.)\nTest                    :   false (Verify DOD root certificates are installed)\nResult Analysis         :        .  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:tst:25156001 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Firefox must have the DOD root certificates installed.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:obj:25156001 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : Retrieve Firefox ImportEnterpriseRoots\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\Certificates'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'ImportEnterpriseRoots'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:ste:25156001 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : Value Equal To 1\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\Certificates'\n                        : name equals 'ImportEnterpriseRoots'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330997290000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:tst:25156002 (cmdlet_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Verify DOD root certificates are installed\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:obj:25156002 (cmdlet_object)\nObject Comment          : Gather root certicates.\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'module_name' must be equal to 'Microsoft.Powershell.Management'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'verb' must be equal to 'Get'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'noun' must be equal to 'ChildItem'\nObject Requirement      : for  'parameters' the following must be true:\n                        : path must be equal to 'Cert:\\LocalMachine\\Root'\nObject Requirement      : for  'select' the following must be true:\n                        : property must be equal to 'issuer,thumbprint'\nInclude Items If        : for at least one 'value' the following must be true:\n                        : all issuer must match the pattern '^CN=DoD Root CA' issuer matches the pattern '^CN=DoD Root CA'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:ste:25156002 (cmdlet_state)\nState Comment           : Cert issuer is DOD Root CA\nState Requirement       : for at least one 'value' the following must be true:\n                        : all issuer must match the pattern '^CN=DoD Root CA.*O=U.S. Government'\n\nResult Analysis         : .  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n"},{"discussion":"There should not be an option for a user to \"forget\" work they have done. This is required to meet non-repudiation controls.","mitigation_control":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:23\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Firefox prevents the user from quickly deleting data)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\DisableForgetButton'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:tst:11700 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Firefox prevents the user from quickly deleting data\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:obj:11700 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisableForgetButton'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:ste:1 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\DisableForgetButton'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n","rule_version":"FFOX-00-000018","comments":null,"uuid":"93E604EB-6BF8-1014-A9EF-93A473DA8B44","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id_src":"SV-251562r987660_rule","responsibility":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-251562","title":"SRG-APP-000326"},"fix_text":"Windows group policy:\n1. Open the group policy editor tool with \"gpedit.msc\".\n2. Navigate to Policy Path: Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Mozilla\\Firefox\nPolicy Name: Disable Forget Button\nPolicy State: Enabled\n\nmacOS \"plist\" file:\nAdd the following:\n&lt;key&gt;DisableForgetButton&lt;/key&gt;\n&lt;true/&gt;\n\nLinux \"policies.json\" file:\nAdd the following in the policies section:\n\"DisableForgetButton\": true","legacy_ids":[],"potential_impacts":"","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5446","rule_id":"SV-251562r987660","mitigations":"","stig_uuid":"93E2B29A-6BF8-1014-B7B8-F59365D05FB5","status":"open","group_id_src":"V-251562","severity":"medium","classification":"Unclassified","group_title":"SRG-APP-000326","check_content":"Type \"about:policies\" in the browser address bar. \n\nIf \"DisableForgetButton\" is not displayed under Policy Name or the Policy Value is not \"true\", this is a finding.","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MOZ_Firefox_Windows_V6R7_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV12-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:def:117"},"ia_controls":"","third_party_tools":"","rule_title":"Firefox must prevent the user from quickly deleting data.","false_positives":"","weight":"10.0","ccis":["CCI-002355"],"group_id":"V-251562"},{"severity":"medium","group_id_src":"V-251563","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:def:118","href":"U_MOZ_Firefox_Windows_V6R7_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV12-oval.xml"},"check_content":"Type \"about:policies\" in the browser window. \n\nIf \"DisablePrivateBrowsing\" is not displayed under Policy Name or the Policy Value is not \"true\", this is a finding.","classification":"Unclassified","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","rule_title":"Firefox private browsing must be disabled.","third_party_tools":"","ia_controls":"","group_id":"V-251563","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"weight":"10.0","false_positives":"","reference_identifier":"5446","documentable":"false","mitigations":"","rule_id":"SV-251563r960963","stig_uuid":"93E2B29A-6BF8-1014-B7B8-F59365D05FB5","status":"open","uuid":"93E60963-6BF8-1014-8EB7-D579CB98E55B","comments":null,"rule_version":"FFOX-00-000019","responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-251563r960963_rule","security_override_guidance":"","group_tree":{"id":"V-251563","title":"SRG-APP-000141"},"fix_text":"Windows group policy:\n1. Open the group policy editor tool with \"gpedit.msc\".\n2. Navigate to Policy Path: Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Mozilla\\Firefox\nPolicy Name: Disable Private Browsing\nPolicy State: Enabled\n\nmacOS \"plist\" file:\nAdd the following:\n&lt;key&gt;DisablePrivateBrowsing&lt;/key&gt;\n&lt;true/&gt;\n\nLinux \"policies.json\" file:\nAdd the following in the policies section:\n\"DisablePrivateBrowsing\": true","potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":[],"mitigation_control":"","discussion":"Private browsing allows the user to browse the internet without recording their browsing history/activity. From a forensics perspective, this is unacceptable. Best practice requires that browser history is retained.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:23\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Firefox private browsing is disabled)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\DisablePrivateBrowsing'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:tst:11800 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Firefox private browsing is disabled\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:obj:11800 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisablePrivateBrowsing'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:ste:1 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\DisablePrivateBrowsing'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n"},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:23\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Firefox search suggestions is disabled)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\SearchSuggestEnabled'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:tst:11900 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Firefox search suggestions is disabled\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:obj:11900 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'SearchSuggestEnabled'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:ste:2 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\SearchSuggestEnabled'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n","mitigation_control":"","discussion":"Search suggestions must be disabled as this could lead to searches being conducted that were never intended to be made.","potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"id":"V-251564","title":"SRG-APP-000141"},"fix_text":"Windows group policy:\n1. Open the group policy editor tool with \"gpedit.msc\".\n2. Navigate to Policy Path: Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\Search\nPolicy Name: Search Suggestions\nPolicy State: Disabled\n\nmacOS \"plist\" file:\nAdd the following:\n&lt;key&gt;SearchSuggestEnabled&lt;/key&gt;\n&lt;false/&gt;\n\nLinux \"policies.json\" file:\nAdd the following in the policies section:\n\"SearchSuggestEnabled\": false","rule_id_src":"SV-251564r960963_rule","responsibility":"","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"93E60E32-6BF8-1014-BAF9-9FBCEEAE99CD","rule_version":"FFOX-00-000020","comments":null,"status":"open","stig_uuid":"93E2B29A-6BF8-1014-B7B8-F59365D05FB5","rule_id":"SV-251564r960963","mitigations":"","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5446","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"group_id":"V-251564","weight":"10.0","false_positives":"","ia_controls":"","rule_title":"Firefox search suggestions must be disabled.","third_party_tools":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:def:119","href":"U_MOZ_Firefox_Windows_V6R7_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV12-oval.xml"},"classification":"Unclassified","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","check_content":"Type \"about:policies\" in the browser window.\n\nIf \"SearchSuggestEnabled\" is not displayed under Policy Name or the Policy Value is not \"false\", this is a finding.","group_id_src":"V-251564","severity":"medium"},{"mitigation_control":"","discussion":"Autoplay allows the user to control whether videos can play automatically (without user consent) with audio content. The user must be able to select content that is run within the browser window.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:23\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Firefox autoplay is disabled)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\Permissions\\Autoplay\\Default'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:tst:12000 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Firefox autoplay is disabled\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:obj:12000 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\Permissions\\Autoplay'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'Default'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:ste:12000 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_sz'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must match the pattern 'block-audio-video'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\Permissions\\Autoplay\\Default'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n","responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-251565r960963_rule","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"93E612E8-6BF8-1014-9A16-EEEDCF31902B","rule_version":"FFOX-00-000021","comments":null,"potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":[],"group_tree":{"id":"V-251565","title":"SRG-APP-000141"},"fix_text":"Windows group policy:\n1. Open the group policy editor tool with \"gpedit.msc\".\n2. Navigate to Policy Path: Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\Permissions\\Autoplay\nPolicy Name: Default autoplay level\nPolicy State: Enabled\nPolicy Value: Block Audio and Video\n\nmacOS \"plist\" file:\nAdd the following:\n&lt;key&gt;Permissions&lt;/key&gt;\n&lt;dict&gt;\n  &lt;key&gt;Autoplay&lt;/key&gt;\n  &lt;dict&gt;\n    &lt;string&gt;block-audio-video&lt;/string&gt;\n  &lt;/dict&gt;\n&lt;/dict&gt;\n \nLinux \"policies.json\" file:\nAdd the following in the policies section:\n\"Permissions\": {\n  \"Autoplay\": {\n    \"Default\": \"block-audio-video\"\n  }\n}","rule_id":"SV-251565r960963","mitigations":"","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5446","status":"open","stig_uuid":"93E2B29A-6BF8-1014-B7B8-F59365D05FB5","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MOZ_Firefox_Windows_V6R7_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV12-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:def:120"},"group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","classification":"Unclassified","check_content":"Type \"about:policies\" in the browser address bar. \n\nIf \"Permissions\" is not displayed under Policy Name or the Policy Value is not \"Autoplay\" with a value of \"Default\" and \"Block-audio-video\", this is a finding.","group_id_src":"V-251565","severity":"low","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"group_id":"V-251565","false_positives":"","weight":"10.0","ia_controls":"","third_party_tools":"","rule_title":"Firefox autoplay must be disabled."},{"fix_text":"Windows group policy:\n1. Open the group policy editor tool with \"gpedit.msc\".\n2. Navigate to Policy Path: Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Mozilla\\Firefox\nPolicy Name: Network Prediction\nPolicy State: Disabled\n\nmacOS \"plist\" file:\nAdd the following:\n&lt;key&gt;NetworkPrediction&lt;/key&gt;\n&lt;false/&gt;\n\nLinux \"policies.json\" file:\nAdd the following in the policies section:\n\"NetworkPrediction\": false","group_tree":{"id":"V-251566","title":"SRG-APP-000141"},"potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":[],"uuid":"93E61771-6BF8-1014-B601-90B7670A36A9","rule_version":"FFOX-00-000022","comments":null,"responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-251566r960963_rule","security_override_guidance":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:23\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Firefox network prediction is disabled)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\NetworkPrediction'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:tst:12100 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Firefox network prediction is disabled\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:obj:12100 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'NetworkPrediction'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:ste:2 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\NetworkPrediction'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n","mitigation_control":"","discussion":"If network prediction is enabled, requests to URLs are made without user consent. The browser should always make a direct DNS request without prefetching occurring.","ia_controls":"","third_party_tools":"","rule_title":"Firefox network prediction must be disabled.","group_id":"V-251566","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"false_positives":"","weight":"10.0","group_id_src":"V-251566","severity":"medium","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MOZ_Firefox_Windows_V6R7_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV12-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:def:121"},"classification":"Unclassified","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","check_content":"Type \"about:policies\" in the browser window. \n\nIf \"NetworkPrediction\" is not displayed under Policy Name or the Policy Value is not \"false\", this is a finding.","stig_uuid":"93E2B29A-6BF8-1014-B7B8-F59365D05FB5","status":"open","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5446","rule_id":"SV-251566r960963","mitigations":""},{"status":"not_a_finding","stig_uuid":"93E2B29A-6BF8-1014-B7B8-F59365D05FB5","rule_id":"SV-251567r960963","mitigations":"","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5446","weight":"10.0","false_positives":"","group_id":"V-251567","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"ia_controls":"","rule_title":"Firefox fingerprinting protection must be enabled.","third_party_tools":"","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","classification":"Unclassified","check_content":"Type \"about:policies\" in the browser address bar. \n\nIf \"EnableTrackingProtection\" is not displayed under Policy Name or the Policy Value is not \"Fingerprinting\"  with a value of \"true\", this is a finding.","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MOZ_Firefox_Windows_V6R7_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV12-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:def:122"},"group_id_src":"V-251567","severity":"medium","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:23\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Firefox fingerprinting protection is enabled)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:tst:12200 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Firefox fingerprinting protection is enabled\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:obj:12200 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\EnableTrackingProtection'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'Fingerprinting'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:ste:1 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\EnableTrackingProtection'\n                        : name equals 'Fingerprinting'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330997290000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","discussion":"The Content Blocking/Tracking Protection feature stops Firefox from loading content from malicious sites. The content might be a script or an image, for example. If a site is on one of the tracker lists that Firefox is set to use, the fingerprinting script (or other tracking script/image) will not be loaded from that site.\n\nFingerprinting scripts collect information about browser and device configuration, such as operating system, screen resolution, and other settings. By compiling these pieces of data, fingerprinters create a unique profile that can be used to track the user around the web.","mitigation_control":"","legacy_ids":[],"potential_impacts":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-251567"},"fix_text":"Windows group policy:\n1. Open the group policy editor tool with \"gpedit.msc\".\n2. Navigate to Policy Path: Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\Tracking Protection\nPolicy Name: Fingerprinting\nPolicy State: Enabled\n\nmacOS \"plist\" file:\nAdd the following:\n&lt;key&gt;EnableTrackingProtection&lt;/key&gt;\n  &lt;dict&gt;\n    &lt;key&gt;Fingerprinting&lt;/key&gt;\n &lt;true/&gt;\n  &lt;/dict&gt;\n\nLinux \"policies.json\" file:\nAdd the following in the policies section:\n\"EnableTrackingProtection\": {\n  \"Fingerprinting\": true\n}","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id_src":"SV-251567r960963_rule","responsibility":"","rule_version":"FFOX-00-000023","comments":null,"uuid":"93E6ABF6-6BF8-1014-87AA-8BB9BD0A5BF5"},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:23\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Firefox Cryptomining protection is enabled)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:tst:12300 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Firefox Cryptomining protection is enabled\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:obj:12300 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\EnableTrackingProtection'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'Cryptomining'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:ste:1 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\EnableTrackingProtection'\n                        : name equals 'Cryptomining'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330997290000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n","mitigation_control":"","discussion":"The Content Blocking/Tracking Protection feature stops Firefox from loading content from malicious sites. The content might be a script or an image, for example. If a site is on one of the tracker lists that Firefox is set to use, the fingerprinting script (or other tracking script/image) will not be loaded from that site.\n\nCryptomining scripts use a computer's central processing unit to invisibly mine cryptocurrency.","potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":[],"fix_text":"Windows group policy:\n1. Open the group policy editor tool with \"gpedit.msc\".\n2. Navigate to Policy Path: Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\Tracking Protection\nPolicy Name: Cryptomining\nPolicy State: Enabled\n\nmacOS \"plist\" file:\nAdd the following:\n&lt;key&gt;EnableTrackingProtection&lt;/key&gt;\n  &lt;dict&gt;\n    &lt;key&gt;Cryptomining&lt;/key&gt;\n &lt;true/&gt;\n  &lt;/dict&gt;\n\nLinux \"policies.json\" file:\nAdd the following in the policies section:\n\"EnableTrackingProtection\": {\n  \"Cryptomining\": true\n}","group_tree":{"id":"V-251568","title":"SRG-APP-000141"},"responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-251568r960963_rule","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"93E6BC37-6BF8-1014-AEE4-C2FDC4D16006","comments":null,"rule_version":"FFOX-00-000024","status":"not_a_finding","stig_uuid":"93E2B29A-6BF8-1014-B7B8-F59365D05FB5","mitigations":"","rule_id":"SV-251568r960963","reference_identifier":"5446","documentable":"false","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"group_id":"V-251568","weight":"10.0","false_positives":"","rule_title":"Firefox cryptomining protection must be enabled.","third_party_tools":"","ia_controls":"","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MOZ_Firefox_Windows_V6R7_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV12-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:def:123"},"check_content":"Type \"about:policies\" in the browser address bar. \n\nIf \"EnableTrackingProtection\" is not displayed under Policy Name or the Policy Value is not \"Cryptomining\" with a value of \"true\", this is a finding.","classification":"Unclassified","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","severity":"medium","group_id_src":"V-251568"},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:23\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Firefox Enhanced Tracking Protection must be enabled.)\nResult Analysis         :        '' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to '\"browser.contentblocking.category\": \\{    \"Value\": \"strict\",    \"Status\": \"locked\"  }' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:tst:25156901 (variable_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Firefox Enhanced Tracking Protection must be enabled.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:obj:25156901 (variable_object)\nObject Comment          : Merged format of Firefox SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\Preferences Multi-String registry key\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'var_ref' must be equal to 'oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:var:25156901'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:ste:25156901 (variable_state)\nState Comment           : browser.contentblocking.category is set to strict and locked\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must match the pattern '\"browser.contentblocking.category\": \\{    \"Value\": \"strict\",    \"Status\": \"locked\"  }'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : var_ref equals 'oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:var:25156901'\n                        : value equals ''\n\nResult Analysis         : '' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to '\"browser.contentblocking.category\": \\{    \"Value\": \"strict\",    \"Status\": \"locked\"  }' \n","discussion":"Tracking generally refers to content, cookies, or scripts that can collect browsing data across multiple sites.\n\nIt is detrimental for applications to provide, or install by default, functionality exceeding requirements or mission objectives. These unnecessary capabilities or services are often overlooked and therefore may remain unsecured. They increase the risk to the platform by providing additional attack vectors.\n\nApplications are capable of providing a wide variety of functions and services. Some of the functions and services, provided by default, may not be necessary to support essential organizational operations (e.g., key missions, functions). \n\nExamples of nonessential capabilities include but are not limited to advertising software or browser plug-ins that are not related to requirements or provide a wide array of functionality not required for every mission but that cannot be disabled.","mitigation_control":"","legacy_ids":[],"potential_impacts":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-251569"},"fix_text":"Windows group policy:\n1. Open the group policy editor tool with \"gpedit.msc\".\n2. Navigate to Policy Path: Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\\nPolicy Name: Preferences\nPolicy State: Enabled\nPolicy Value:\n{\n  \"browser.contentblocking.category\": {\n    \"Value\": \"strict\",\n    \"Status\": \"locked\"\n  }\n}\n\nmacOS \"plist\" file:\nAdd the following:\n&lt;key&gt;Preferences&lt;/key&gt;\n&lt;dict&gt;\n  &lt;key&gt;browser.contentblocking.category&lt;/key&gt;\n  &lt;dict&gt;\n    &lt;key&gt;Value&lt;/key&gt;\n    &lt;string&gt;strict&lt;/string&gt;\n    &lt;key&gt;Status&lt;/key&gt;\n    &lt;string&gt;locked&lt;/string&gt;\n  &lt;/dict&gt;\n&lt;/dict&gt;\n\nLinux \"policies.json\" file:\nAdd the following in the policies section:\n\"Preferences\": {\n  \"browser.contentblocking.category\": {\n    \"Value\": \"strict\",\n    \"Status\": \"locked\"\n  }\n}","security_override_guidance":"","responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-251569r1067561_rule","rule_version":"FFOX-00-000025","comments":null,"uuid":"93E6C64C-6BF8-1014-BF43-B40D57E429BC","status":"open","stig_uuid":"93E2B29A-6BF8-1014-B7B8-F59365D05FB5","rule_id":"SV-251569r1067561","mitigations":"","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5446","weight":"10.0","false_positives":"","group_id":"V-251569","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"ia_controls":"","rule_title":"Firefox Enhanced Tracking Protection must be enabled.","third_party_tools":"","classification":"Unclassified","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","check_content":"Type \"about:policies\" in the browser address bar. \n\nIf \"Preferences\" is not displayed under Policy Name or the Policy Value does not include \"browser.contentblocking.category\" with a value of  \"strict\" and status of \"locked\", this is a finding.","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:def:251569","href":"U_MOZ_Firefox_Windows_V6R7_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV12-oval2.xml"},"group_id_src":"V-251569","severity":"medium"},{"check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MOZ_Firefox_Windows_V6R7_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV12-oval2.xml","name":"oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:def:251570"},"group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","classification":"Unclassified","check_content":"Type \"about:policies\" in the browser address bar. \n\nIf \"Preferences\" is not displayed under Policy Name and the Policy Value does not include \"extensions.htmlaboutaddons.recommendations.enabled\" with a value of  \"false\" and status of \"locked\", this is a finding.","group_id_src":"V-251570","severity":"medium","group_id":"V-251570","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"false_positives":"","weight":"10.0","ia_controls":"","third_party_tools":"","rule_title":"Firefox extension recommendations must be disabled.","rule_id":"SV-251570r1067563","mitigations":"","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5446","status":"open","stig_uuid":"93E2B29A-6BF8-1014-B7B8-F59365D05FB5","responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-251570r1067563_rule","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"93E6CFCC-6BF8-1014-ABF3-BA4566608470","rule_version":"FFOX-00-000026","comments":null,"potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":[],"fix_text":"Windows group policy:\n1. Open the group policy editor tool with \"gpedit.msc\".\n2. Navigate to Policy Path: Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\\nPolicy Name: Preferences\nPolicy State: Enabled\nPolicy Value:\n{\n  \"extensions.htmlaboutaddons.recommendations.enabled\": {\n    \"Value\": false,\n    \"Status\": \"locked\"\n  }\n}\n\nmacOS \"plist\" file:\nAdd the following:\n&lt;key&gt;Preferences&lt;/key&gt;\n&lt;dict&gt;\n  &lt;key&gt;extensions.htmlaboutaddons.recommendations.enabled&lt;/key&gt;\n  &lt;dict&gt;\n    &lt;key&gt;Value&lt;/key&gt;\n    &lt;false/&gt;\n    &lt;key&gt;Status&lt;/key&gt;\n    &lt;string&gt;locked&lt;/string&gt;\n  &lt;/dict&gt;\n&lt;/dict&gt;\n\nLinux \"policies.json\" file:\nAdd the following in the policies section:\n\"Preferences\": {\n\"extensions.htmlaboutaddons.recommendations.enabled\": {\n\"Value\": false,\n\"Status\": \"locked\"\n},","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-251570"},"mitigation_control":"","discussion":"The Recommended Extensions program makes it easier for users to discover extensions that have been reviewed for security, functionality, and user experience. Allowed extensions are to be centrally managed.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:23\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Firefox extension recommendations must be disabled.)\nResult Analysis         :        '' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to '\"extensions.htmlaboutaddons.recommendations.enabled\": \\{    \"Value\": false,    \"Status\": \"locked\"  }' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:tst:25157001 (variable_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Firefox extension recommendations must be disabled.\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:obj:25157001 (variable_object)\nObject Comment          : Merged format of Firefox SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\Preferences Multi-String registry key\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'var_ref' must be equal to 'oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:var:25157001'\n\nState ID                : oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:ste:25157001 (variable_state)\nState Comment           : Verify extensions.htmlaboutaddons.recommendations.enabled is set to false and locked\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must match the pattern '\"extensions.htmlaboutaddons.recommendations.enabled\": \\{    \"Value\": false,    \"Status\": \"locked\"  }'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : var_ref equals 'oval:navy.navwar.niwcatlantic.scc.firefox.windows:var:25157001'\n                        : value equals ''\n\nResult Analysis         : '' failed test of 'pattern match' compared to '\"extensions.htmlaboutaddons.recommendations.enabled\": \\{    \"Value\": false,    \"Status\": \"locked\"  }' \n"},{"stig_uuid":"93E2B29A-6BF8-1014-B7B8-F59365D05FB5","status":"open","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5446","rule_id":"SV-251571r960963","mitigations":"","ia_controls":"","rule_title":"Firefox deprecated ciphers must be disabled.","third_party_tools":"","weight":"10.0","false_positives":"","group_id":"V-251571","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"group_id_src":"V-251571","severity":"medium","classification":"Unclassified","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","check_content":"Type \"about:policies\" in the browser address bar.\n\nIf \"DisabledCiphers\" is not displayed under Policy Name or the Policy Value is not \"TLS_RSA_WITH_3DES_EDE_CBC_SHA\" with a value of  \"true\", this is a finding.","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:def:126","href":"U_MOZ_Firefox_Windows_V6R7_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV12-oval.xml"},"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:23\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Firefox deprecated ciphers are disabled)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\DisabledCiphers\\TLS_RSA_WITH_3DES_EDE_CBC_SHA'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:tst:12600 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Firefox deprecated ciphers are disabled\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:obj:12600 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\DisabledCiphers'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'TLS_RSA_WITH_3DES_EDE_CBC_SHA'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:ste:1 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\DisabledCiphers\\TLS_RSA_WITH_3DES_EDE_CBC_SHA'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n","discussion":"A weak cipher is defined as an encryption/decryption algorithm that uses a key of insufficient length. Using an insufficient length for a key in an encryption/decryption algorithm opens up the possibility (or probability) that the encryption scheme could be broken.","mitigation_control":"","fix_text":"Windows group policy:\n1. Open the group policy editor tool with \"gpedit.msc\".\n2. Navigate to Policy Path: Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\Disabled Ciphers\nPolicy Name: TLS_RSA_WITH_3DES_EDE_CBC_SHA\nPolicy State: Enabled\n\nmacOS \"plist\" file:\nAdd the following:\n&lt;key&gt;DisabledCiphers&lt;/key&gt;\n  &lt;dict&gt;\n    &lt;key&gt;TLS_RSA_WITH_3DES_EDE_CBC_SHA&lt;/key&gt;\n    &lt;true/&gt;\n  &lt;/dict&gt;\n\nLinux \"policies.json\" file:\nAdd the following in the policies section:\n\"DisabledCiphers\": {\n  \"TLS_RSA_WITH_3DES_EDE_CBC_SHA\": true\n}","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-251571"},"legacy_ids":[],"potential_impacts":"","rule_version":"FFOX-00-000027","comments":null,"uuid":"93E6D8D8-6BF8-1014-BCAA-DF60C8AF547A","security_override_guidance":"","responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-251571r960963_rule"},{"group_id_src":"V-251572","severity":"medium","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","classification":"Unclassified","check_content":"Type \"about:policies\" in the browser address bar. \n\nIf \"UserMessaging\" is not displayed under Policy Name or the Policy Value is not \"ExtensionRecommendations\" with a value of \"false\", this is a finding.","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MOZ_Firefox_Windows_V6R7_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV12-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:def:127"},"ia_controls":"","rule_title":"Firefox must not recommend extensions as the user is using the browser.","third_party_tools":"","false_positives":"","weight":"10.0","group_id":"V-251572","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5446","rule_id":"SV-251572r960963","mitigations":"","stig_uuid":"93E2B29A-6BF8-1014-B7B8-F59365D05FB5","status":"not_a_finding","rule_version":"FFOX-00-000028","comments":null,"uuid":"93E6E66F-6BF8-1014-B5A5-A4A04A44FD51","security_override_guidance":"","responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-251572r960963_rule","fix_text":"Windows group policy:\n1. Open the group policy editor tool with \"gpedit.msc\".\n2. Navigate to Policy Path: Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\User Messaging\nPolicy Name: Extension Recommendations\nPolicy State: Disabled\n\nmacOS \"plist\" file:\nAdd the following:\n&lt;key&gt;UserMessaging&lt;/key&gt;\n&lt;dict&gt;\n  &lt;key&gt;ExtensionRecommendations&lt;/key&gt;\n  &lt;false/&gt;\n&lt;/dict&gt;\n\nLinux \"policies.json\" file:\nAdd the following in the policies section:\n\"UserMessaging\": {\n  \"ExtensionRecommendations\": false\n}","group_tree":{"id":"V-251572","title":"SRG-APP-000141"},"legacy_ids":[],"potential_impacts":"","discussion":"The Recommended Extensions program recommends extensions to users as they surf the web.\n\nThe user must not be encouraged to install extensions from the websites they visit. Allowed extensions are to be centrally managed.","mitigation_control":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:23\nResult: passRule Result             : Pass\nCriteria                : true (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   true (Firefox does not recommend extensions as the user is using the browser)\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:tst:12700 (registry_test)\nResult                  : true\nTest Title              : Firefox does not recommend extensions as the user is using the browser\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:obj:12700 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\UserMessaging'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'ExtensionRecommendations'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:ste:2 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : true\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\UserMessaging'\n                        : name equals 'ExtensionRecommendations'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330997290000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '0'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n"},{"potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":[],"fix_text":"Windows group policy:\n1. Open the group policy editor tool with \"gpedit.msc\".\n2. Navigate to Policy Path: Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Mozilla\\Firefox\nPolicy Name: Customize Firefox Home\nPolicy State: Enabled\nPolicy Value: Uncheck \"Search\"\nPolicy Value: Uncheck \"Top Sites\"\nPolicy Value: Uncheck \"Sponsored Top Sites\"\nPolicy Value: Uncheck \"Recommended by Pocket\"\nPolicy Value: Uncheck \"Sponsored Pocket Stories\"\nPolicy Value: Uncheck \"Download History\"\nPolicy Value: Uncheck \"Snippets\"\nPolicy Value: Check \"Do not allow settings to be changed\"\n\nmacOS \"plist\" file:\nAdd the following:\n&lt;key&gt;FirefoxHome&lt;/key&gt;\n&lt;dict&gt;\n&lt;key&gt;Search&lt;/key&gt;\n  &lt;false/&gt;\n&lt;key&gt;TopSites&lt;/key&gt;\n  &lt;false/&gt;\n&lt;key&gt;SponsoredTopSites&lt;/key&gt;\n  &lt;false/&gt;\n&lt;key&gt;Pocket&lt;/key&gt;\n  &lt;false/&gt;\n&lt;key&gt;SponsoredPocket&lt;/key&gt;\n  &lt;false/&gt;\n&lt;key&gt;Highlights&lt;/key&gt;\n  &lt;false/&gt;\n&lt;key&gt;Snippets&lt;/key&gt;\n  &lt;false/&gt;\n&lt;key&gt;Locked&lt;/key&gt;\n  &lt;true/&gt;\n&lt;/dict&gt;\n\nLinux \"policies.json\" file:\nAdd the following in the policies section:\n\"FirefoxHome\": {\n  \"Search\": false,\n  \"TopSites\": false,\n  \"SponsoredTopSites\": false,\n  \"Pocket\": false,\n  \"SponsoredPocket\": false,\n  \"Highlights\": false,\n  \"Snippets\": false,\n  \"locked\": true\n}","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-251573"},"responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-251573r960963_rule","security_override_guidance":"","uuid":"93E6ECD8-6BF8-1014-BB01-C503F51EF1C6","rule_version":"FFOX-00-000029","comments":null,"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:23\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (The Firefox New Tab page does not show Top Sites)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\FirefoxHome\\TopSites'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :   false (The Firefox New Tab page does not show Sponsored Top Sites)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\FirefoxHome\\SponsoredTopSites'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :   false (The Firefox New Tab page does not show Pocket Recommendations)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\FirefoxHome\\Pocket'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :   false (The Firefox New Tab page does not show Sponsored Pocket Stories)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\FirefoxHome\\SponsoredPocket'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :  