t                  : false\nTest Title              : The Firefox New Tab page does not show Snippets\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:obj:12805 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\FirefoxHome'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'Snippets'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:ste:2 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\FirefoxHome\\Snippets'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:tst:12806 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Customize Firefox Home settings are locked\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:obj:12806 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\FirefoxHome'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'Locked'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:ste:1 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\FirefoxHome\\Locked'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:tst:12807 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : The Firefox New Tab page does not show Search\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:obj:12807 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\FirefoxHome'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'Search'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:ste:2 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\FirefoxHome\\Search'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n","mitigation_control":"","discussion":"The New Tab page by default shows a list of built-in top sites, as well as the top sites the user has visited.\n\nIt is detrimental for applications to provide, or install by default, functionality exceeding requirements or mission objectives. These unnecessary capabilities or services are often overlooked and therefore may remain unsecured. They increase the risk to the platform by providing additional attack vectors.\n\nApplications are capable of providing a wide variety of functions and services. Some of the functions and services, provided by default, may not be necessary to support essential organizational operations (e.g., key missions, functions). \n\nExamples of non-essential capabilities include but are not limited to advertising software or browser plug-ins that are not related to requirements or provide a wide array of functionality not required for every mission but that cannot be disabled.\n\nThe new tab page must not actively show user activity.","group_id":"V-251573","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"false_positives":"","weight":"10.0","ia_controls":"","rule_title":"The Firefox New Tab page must not show Top Sites, Sponsored Top Sites, Pocket Recommendations, Sponsored Pocket Stories, Searches, Highlights, or Snippets.","third_party_tools":"","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:def:128","href":"U_MOZ_Firefox_Windows_V6R7_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV12-oval.xml"},"classification":"Unclassified","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","check_content":"Type \"about:policies\" in the browser address bar. \n\nIf \"FirefoxHome\" is not displayed under Policy Name or the Policy Value does not have \"Search\" with a value of \"false\", this is a finding.\nIf \"FirefoxHome\" is not displayed under Policy Name or the Policy Value does not have \"TopSites\" with a value of \"false\", this is a finding.\nIf \"FirefoxHome\" is not displayed under Policy Name or the Policy Value does not have \"SponsoredTopSites\" with a value of \"false\", this is a finding.\nIf \"FirefoxHome\" is not displayed under Policy Name or the Policy Value does not have \"Pocket\" with a value of \"false\", this is a finding.\nIf \"FirefoxHome\" is not displayed under Policy Name or the Policy Value does not have \"SponsoredPocket\" with a value of \"false\", this is a finding.\nIf \"FirefoxHome\" is not displayed under Policy Name or the Policy Value does not have \"Highlights\" with a value of \"false\", this is a finding.\nIf \"FirefoxHome\" is not displayed under Policy Name or the Policy Value does not have \"Snippets\" with a value of \"false\", this is a finding.\nIf \"FirefoxHome\" is not displayed under Policy Name or the Policy Value does not have \"Locked\" with a value of \"true\", this is a finding.","group_id_src":"V-251573","severity":"medium","status":"open","stig_uuid":"93E2B29A-6BF8-1014-B7B8-F59365D05FB5","rule_id":"SV-251573r960963","mitigations":"","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5446"},{"group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","classification":"Unclassified","check_content":"Type \"about:policies\" in the browser address bar. \n\nIf \"DNSOverHTTPS\" is not displayed under Policy Name or the Policy Value does not have \"Enabled\" with a value of \"false\", this is a finding.","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:def:132","href":"U_MOZ_Firefox_Windows_V6R7_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV12-oval.xml"},"group_id_src":"V-251577","severity":"medium","false_positives":"","weight":"10.0","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"group_id":"V-251577","ia_controls":"","third_party_tools":"","rule_title":"Firefox must be configured so that DNS over HTTPS is disabled.","rule_id":"SV-251577r960963","mitigations":"","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5446","status":"open","stig_uuid":"93E2B29A-6BF8-1014-B7B8-F59365D05FB5","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id_src":"SV-251577r960963_rule","responsibility":"","rule_version":"FFOX-00-000033","comments":null,"uuid":"93E6F1EA-6BF8-1014-84F4-DB3EF0D46EA9","legacy_ids":[],"potential_impacts":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-251577"},"fix_text":"Windows group policy:\n1. Open the group policy editor tool with \"gpedit.msc\".\n2. Navigate to Policy Path: Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\DNS Over HTTPS\nPolicy Name: Enabled\nPolicy State: Disabled\n\nmacOS \"plist\" file:\n&lt;key&gt;DNSOverHTTPS&lt;/key&gt;\n  &lt;dict&gt;\n    &lt;key&gt;Enabled&lt;/key&gt;\n    &lt;false/&gt;\n\nLinux \"policies.json\" file:\nAdd the following in the policies section:\n\"DNSOverHTTPS\": {\"Enabled\": false}","discussion":"DNS over HTTPS has generally not been adopted in the DoD. DNS is tightly controlled.\n\nIt is detrimental for applications to provide, or install by default, functionality exceeding requirements or mission objectives. These unnecessary capabilities or services are often overlooked and therefore may remain unsecured. They increase the risk to the platform by providing additional attack vectors.\n\nApplications are capable of providing a wide variety of functions and services. Some of the functions and services, provided by default, may not be necessary to support essential organizational operations (e.g., key missions, functions). \n\nExamples of non-essential capabilities include, but are not limited to, advertising software or browser plug-ins not related to requirements or providing a wide array of functionality not required for every mission, but cannot be disabled.","mitigation_control":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:23\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Firefox is configured so that DNS over HTTPS is disabled)\nResult Analysis         :        HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\DNSOverHTTPS\\Enabled\\value = '1' failed test of 'equals' compared to '0' \n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:tst:13200 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Firefox is configured so that DNS over HTTPS is disabled\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:obj:13200 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\DNSOverHTTPS'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'Enabled'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:ste:2 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nCollected Item/State Result : false\n                        : hive equals 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\n                        : key equals 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\DNSOverHTTPS'\n                        : name equals 'Enabled'\n                        : last_write_time equals '134330997290000000'\n                        : type equals 'reg_dword'\n                        : value equals '1'\n                        : windows_view equals '64_bit'\n\nResult Analysis         : HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\DNSOverHTTPS\\Enabled\\value = '1' failed test of 'equals' compared to '0' \n"},{"finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:23\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Firefox accounts are disabled)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\DisableFirefoxAccounts'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:tst:13300 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Firefox accounts are disabled\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:obj:13300 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisableFirefoxAccounts'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:ste:1 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\DisableFirefoxAccounts'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n","discussion":"Disable Firefox Accounts integration (Sync). \n\nIt is detrimental for applications to provide, or install by default, functionality exceeding requirements or mission objectives. These unnecessary capabilities or services are often overlooked and therefore may remain unsecured. They increase the risk to the platform by providing additional attack vectors.\n\nApplications are capable of providing a wide variety of functions and services. Some of the functions and services, provided by default, may not be necessary to support essential organizational operations (e.g., key missions, functions). \n\nExamples of non-essential capabilities include but are not limited to advertising software or browser plug-ins that are not related to requirements or provide a wide array of functionality not required for every mission but that cannot be disabled.","mitigation_control":"","legacy_ids":[],"potential_impacts":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-251578"},"fix_text":"Windows group policy:\n1. Open the group policy editor tool with \"gpedit.msc\".\n2. Navigate to Policy Path: Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\\nPolicy Name: Disable Firefox Accounts\nPolicy State: Enabled\n\nmacOS \"plist\" file:\n&lt;key&gt;DisableFirefoxAccounts&lt;/key&gt;\n  &lt;true/&gt; \n\nLinux \"policies.json\" file:\nAdd the following in the policies section:\n\"DisableFirefoxAccounts\": true","security_override_guidance":"","rule_id_src":"SV-251578r960963_rule","responsibility":"","rule_version":"FFOX-00-000034","comments":null,"uuid":"93E6F697-6BF8-1014-983A-8B3D8F59C78B","status":"open","stig_uuid":"93E2B29A-6BF8-1014-B7B8-F59365D05FB5","rule_id":"SV-251578r960963","mitigations":"","documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5446","false_positives":"","weight":"10.0","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"group_id":"V-251578","ia_controls":"","third_party_tools":"","rule_title":"Firefox accounts must be disabled.","classification":"Unclassified","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","check_content":"Type \"about:policies\" in the browser address bar. \n\nIf \"DisableFirefoxAccounts\" is not displayed under Policy Name or the Policy Value is not \"true\", this is a finding.","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:def:133","href":"U_MOZ_Firefox_Windows_V6R7_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV12-oval.xml"},"group_id_src":"V-251578","severity":"medium"},{"severity":"medium","group_id_src":"V-251580","check_content_ref":{"name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:def:135","href":"U_MOZ_Firefox_Windows_V6R7_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV12-oval.xml"},"check_content":"Type \"about:policies\" in the browser address bar. \n\nIf \"DisableFeedbackCommands\" is not displayed under Policy Name or the Policy Value is not \"true\", this is a finding.","classification":"Unclassified","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","rule_title":"Firefox feedback reporting must be disabled.","third_party_tools":"","ia_controls":"","group_id":"V-251580","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"weight":"10.0","false_positives":"","reference_identifier":"5446","documentable":"false","mitigations":"","rule_id":"SV-251580r960963","stig_uuid":"93E2B29A-6BF8-1014-B7B8-F59365D05FB5","status":"open","uuid":"93E7974A-6BF8-1014-8D7E-E4035DEB637E","comments":null,"rule_version":"FFOX-00-000036","responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-251580r960963_rule","security_override_guidance":"","fix_text":"Windows group policy:\n1. Open the group policy editor tool with \"gpedit.msc\".\n2. Navigate to Policy Path: Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\\nPolicy Name: Disable Feedback Commands\nPolicy State: Enabled\n\nmacOS \"plist\" file:\n&lt;key&gt;DisableFeedbackCommands&lt;/key&gt;\n  &lt;true/&gt;\n\nLinux \"policies.json\" file:\nAdd the following in the policies section:\n\"DisableFeedbackCommands\": true","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-251580"},"potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":[],"mitigation_control":"","discussion":"Disable the menus for reporting sites (Submit Feedback, Report Deceptive Site). \n\nIt is detrimental for applications to provide, or install by default, functionality exceeding requirements or mission objectives. These unnecessary capabilities or services are often overlooked and therefore may remain unsecured. They increase the risk to the platform by providing additional attack vectors.\n\nApplications are capable of providing a wide variety of functions and services. Some of the functions and services, provided by default, may not be necessary to support essential organizational operations (e.g., key missions, functions). \n\nExamples of non-essential capabilities include but are not limited to advertising software or browser plug-ins that are not related to requirements or provide a wide array of functionality not required for every mission but that cannot be disabled.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:23\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Firefox feedback reporting is disabled)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\DisableFeedbackCommands'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:tst:13500 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Firefox feedback reporting is disabled\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:obj:13500 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'DisableFeedbackCommands'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:ste:1 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\DisableFeedbackCommands'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n"},{"documentable":"false","reference_identifier":"5446","rule_id":"SV-251581r960963","mitigations":"","stig_uuid":"93E2B29A-6BF8-1014-B7B8-F59365D05FB5","status":"open","group_id_src":"V-251581","severity":"medium","check_content_ref":{"href":"U_MOZ_Firefox_Windows_V6R7_STIG_SCAP_1-4_Benchmark-enhancedV12-oval.xml","name":"oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:def:136"},"classification":"Unclassified","group_title":"SRG-APP-000141","check_content":"Type \"about:policies\" in the browser address bar. \n\nIf \"EncryptedMediaExtensions\" is not displayed under Policy Name or the Policy Value does not have \"Enabled\" set to \"false\" or the Policy Value does not have \"Locked\" set to \"true\", this is a finding.","ia_controls":"","rule_title":"Firefox encrypted media extensions must be disabled.","third_party_tools":"","ccis":["CCI-000381"],"group_id":"V-251581","false_positives":"","weight":"10.0","mitigation_control":"","discussion":"Enable or disable Encrypted Media Extensions and optionally lock it.\n\nIf \"Enabled\" is set to \"false\", Firefox does not download encrypted media extensions (such as Widevine) unless the user consents to installing them.\n\nIf \"Locked\" is set to \"true\" and \"Enabled\" is set to \"false\", Firefox will not download encrypted media extensions (such as Widevine) or ask the user to install them.\n\nIt is detrimental for applications to provide, or install by default, functionality exceeding requirements or mission objectives. These unnecessary capabilities or services are often overlooked and therefore may remain unsecured. They increase the risk to the platform by providing additional attack vectors.\n\nApplications are capable of providing a wide variety of functions and services. Some of the functions and services, provided by default, may not be necessary to support essential organizational operations (e.g., key missions, functions). \n\nExamples of non-essential capabilities include but are not limited to advertising software or browser plug-ins that are not related to requirements or provide a wide array of functionality not required for every mission but that cannot be disabled.","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:23\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Firefox encrypted media extensions are disabled)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\EncryptedMediaExtensions\\Enabled'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :   false (Firefox encrypted media extensions setting is locked)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\EncryptedMediaExtensions\\Locked'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:tst:13600 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Firefox encrypted media extensions are disabled\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:obj:13600 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\EncryptedMediaExtensions'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'Enabled'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:ste:2 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '0'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\EncryptedMediaExtensions\\Enabled'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:tst:13601 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Firefox encrypted media extensions setting is locked\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:obj:13601 (registry_object)\nObject Comment          : \nObject Requirement      :  check =  'hive' must be equal to 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'key' must be equal to 'SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\EncryptedMediaExtensions'\nObject Requirement      :  check =  'name' must be equal to 'Locked'\n\nState ID                : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:ste:1 (registry_state)\nState Comment           : \nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'type' must be equal to 'reg_dword'\nState Requirement       : check_existence = 'at_least_one_exists',  check = all 'value' must be equal to '1'\n\nResult Analysis         : Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\EncryptedMediaExtensions\\Locked'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n","uuid":"93E7A58A-6BF8-1014-991E-A309A4F808DB","rule_version":"FFOX-00-000037","comments":null,"rule_id_src":"SV-251581r960963_rule","responsibility":"","security_override_guidance":"","fix_text":"Windows group policy:\n1. Open the group policy editor tool with \"gpedit.msc\".\n2. Navigate to Policy Path: Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\Encrypted Media Extensions\nPolicy Name: Enable Encrypted Media Extensions\nPolicy State: Disabled\nPolicy Name: Lock Encrypted Media Extensions\nPolicy State: Enabled\n\nmacOS \"plist\" file:\n&lt;key&gt;EncryptedMediaExtensions&lt;/key&gt;\n  &lt;dict&gt;\n    &lt;key&gt;Enabled&lt;/key&gt;\n    &lt;false/&gt;\n    &lt;key&gt;Locked&lt;/key&gt;\n    &lt;true/&gt; \n\nLinux \"policies.json\" file:\nAdd the following in the policies section:\n\"EncryptedMediaExtensions\": {\n  \"Enabled\": false,\n  \"Locked\": true\n}","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-251581"},"potential_impacts":"","legacy_ids":[]},{"security_override_guidance":"","responsibility":"","rule_id_src":"SV-252881r960963_rule","comments":null,"rule_version":"FFOX-00-000017","uuid":"93E7CBD3-6BF8-1014-89E7-FB2A4E293499","legacy_ids":[],"potential_impacts":"","group_tree":{"title":"SRG-APP-000141","id":"V-252881"},"fix_text":"Windows group policy:\n1. Open the group policy editor tool with \"gpedit.msc\".\n2. Navigate to Policy Path: Computer Configuration\\Administrative Templates\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\Clear data when browser is closed\nPolicy Name: Cache, Cookies, Download History, Form &amp; Search History, Browsing History, Active Logins, Site Preferences, Offline Website Data\nPolicy State: Disabled\nPolicy Name: Locked\nPolicy State: Enabled\n\nmacOS \"plist\" file:\nAdd the following:\n&lt;key&gt;SanitizeOnShutdown&lt;/key&gt;\n&lt;dict&gt;\n  &lt;key&gt;Cache&lt;/key&gt;\n  &lt;false/&gt;\n  &lt;key&gt;Cookies&lt;/key&gt;\n  &lt;false/&gt;\n  &lt;key&gt;Downloads&lt;/key&gt;\n  &lt;false/&gt;\n  &lt;key&gt;FormData&lt;/key&gt;\n  &lt;false/&gt;\n  &lt;key&gt;History&lt;/key&gt;\n  &lt;false/&gt;\n  &lt;key&gt;Sessions&lt;/key&gt;\n  &lt;false/&gt;\n  &lt;key&gt;SiteSettings&lt;/key&gt;\n  &lt;false/&gt;\n  &lt;key&gt;OfflineApps&lt;/key&gt;\n  &lt;false/&gt;\n  &lt;key&gt;Locked&lt;/key&gt;\n  &lt;true/&gt;\n&lt;/dict&gt;\n\nLinux \"policies.json\" file:\nAdd the following in the policies section:\n\"SanitizeOnShutdown\": {\n  \"Cache\": false,\n  \"Cookies\": false,\n  \"Downloads\": false,\n  \"FormData\": false,\n  \"History\": false,\n  \"Sessions\": false,\n  \"SiteSettings\": false,\n  \"OfflineApps\": false,\n  \"Locked\": true \n}","discussion":"For diagnostic purposes, data must remain behind when the browser is closed. This is required to meet non-repudiation controls.","mitigation_control":"","finding_details":"Tool: cpe:/a:niwc:scc:5.14.1\nTime         : 2026-09-05T10:13:23\nResult: failRule Result             : Fail\nCriteria                : false (All child tests must be true. (AND))\nTest                    :   false (Firefox is configured to not delete Cache upon shutdown)\nResult Analysis         :        HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\SanitizeOnShutdown\\Cache\\value = '1' failed test of 'equals' compared to '0' \nTest                    :   false (Firefox is configured to not delete Cookies upon shutdown)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\SanitizeOnShutdown\\Cookies'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :   false (Firefox is configured to not delete Download History upon shutdown)\nResult Analysis         :        HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\SanitizeOnShutdown\\Downloads\\value = '1' failed test of 'equals' compared to '0' \nTest                    :   false (Firefox is configured to not delete Form &amp; Search History upon shutdown)\nResult Analysis         :        HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\SanitizeOnShutdown\\FormData\\value = '1' failed test of 'equals' compared to '0' \nTest                    :   false (Firefox is configured to not delete Browsing History upon shutdown)\nResult Analysis         :        HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\SanitizeOnShutdown\\History\\value = '1' failed test of 'equals' compared to '0' \nTest                    :   false (Firefox is configured to not delete Active Logins upon shutdown)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\SanitizeOnShutdown\\Sessions'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :   false (Firefox is configured to not delete Site Preferences upon shutdown)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\SanitizeOnShutdown\\SiteSettings'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\nTest                    :   false (Firefox is configured to not delete Offline Website Data upon shutdown)\nResult Analysis         :        HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\SanitizeOnShutdown\\OfflineApps\\value = '1' failed test of 'equals' compared to '0' \nTest                    :   false (Firefox SanitizeOnShutdown settings are locked)\nResult Analysis         :        Registry Name Not found: 'HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\\SOFTWARE\\Policies\\Mozilla\\Firefox\\SanitizeOnShutdown\\Locked'.  Existence requirement is 'at_least_one_exists' and no items were collected, so result is false.\n\n---\n\nTest ID                 : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:tst:11600 (registry_test)\nResult                  : false\nTest Title              : Firefox is configured to not delete Cache upon shutdown\nCheck Existence         : One or more collected items must exist.\nCheck                   : All collected items must match the given state(s).\n\nObject ID               : oval:mil.disa.stig.firefox.windows:obj:11600 (registry_object